2026-09-14 18:xx | FIX-IN-PROGRESS | aura-clone: JS bundle SyntaxError identified. Browser receives `Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected token ')'` at assets/index-CugVVnIU.js line 1797 col 45895. Module loads (HTTP 200, correct content-type, full 1.38MB content verified) but DOES NOT EXECUTE top-level code — `createRoot()` never called, root div stays empty. BASE_PATH fix (aa5619a) added to code.html but insufficient alone. Root cause: 9 non-ASCII Unicode chars in bundle (en-dash U+2013, copyright U+00A9, multiplication sign U+00D7, ellipsis U+2026, warning emoji U+26A0+U+FE0F, right single quote U+2019) inside string literals cause V8 ES module parser to reject the file silently. node --check passes (CommonJS mode) but V8 module mode is stricter. Fix path: Vite build must escape non-ASCII chars (configure @rollup/plugin-terser with format: 'cjs' + ascii_only, or terser output.ascii_only=true, or rollup output.banner to force ASCII). This is a BUILD-TIME fix requiring Vite config edit + rebuild + redeploy. NOT a source code fix. Subagent delegation attempted (delegate_task failed with JSON parse errors); headless VS Code agent required for Vite config edit + rebuild. OPS_LOG appended; backup cron will capture. ⟦SIGNED: hermes | nous | poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free⟧

